"DBSIZE" {:fn-name "dbsize", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["DBSIZE"], :fn-docstring "`DBSIZE` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of keys in the database.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/dbsize/"}
"DEBUG" {:fn-name "debug", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1], :req-args-fixed ["DEBUG" arg1], :fn-docstring "`DEBUG` Redis command.\n\nA container for debugging commands.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: Depends on subcommand.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/debug/"}
"DECR" {:fn-name "decr", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["DECR" key], :fn-docstring "`DECR` Redis command.\n\nDecrements the integer value of a key by one. Uses 0 as initial value if the key doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/decr/"}
"DECRBY" {:fn-name "decrby", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key decrement], :req-args-fixed ["DECRBY" key decrement], :fn-docstring "`DECRBY` Redis command.\n\nDecrements a number from the integer value of a key. Uses 0 as initial value if the key doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/decrby/"}
"DEL" {:fn-name "del", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["DEL" key], :fn-docstring "`DEL` Redis command.\n\nDeletes one or more keys.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of keys that will be removed. When a key to remove holds a value other than a string, the individual complexity for this key is O(M) where M is the number of elements in the list, set, sorted set or hash. Removing a single key that holds a string value is O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/del/"}
"DELEX" {:fn-name "delex", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["DELEX" key], :fn-docstring "`DELEX` Redis command.\n\nConditionally removes the specified key based on value or digest comparison.\n\nSince Redis 8.4.0. Complexity: O(1) for IFEQ/IFNE, O(N) for IFDEQ/IFDNE where N is the length of the string value.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/delex/"}
"DIGEST" {:fn-name "digest", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["DIGEST" key], :fn-docstring "`DIGEST` Redis command.\n\nReturns the XXH3 hash of a string value.\n\nSince Redis 8.4.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the length of the string value.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/digest/"}
"DISCARD" {:fn-name "discard", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["DISCARD"], :fn-docstring "`DISCARD` Redis command.\n\nDiscards a transaction.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(N), when N is the number of queued commands.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/discard/"}
"DUMP" {:fn-name "dump", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["DUMP" key], :fn-docstring "`DUMP` Redis command.\n\nReturns a serialized representation of the value stored at a key.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(1) to access the key and additional O(N*M) to serialize it, where N is the number of Redis objects composing the value and M their average size. For small string values the time complexity is thus O(1)+O(1*M) where M is small, so simply O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/dump/"}
"ECHO" {:fn-name "echo", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [message], :req-args-fixed ["ECHO" message], :fn-docstring "`ECHO` Redis command.\n\nReturns the given string.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/echo/"}
