"REPLICAOF" {:fn-name "replicaof", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [arg1 arg2], :req-args-fixed ["REPLICAOF" arg1 arg2], :fn-docstring "`REPLICAOF` Redis command.\n\nConfigures a server as replica of another, or promotes it to a master.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/replicaof/"}
"RESET" {:fn-name "reset", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["RESET"], :fn-docstring "`RESET` Redis command.\n\nResets the connection.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/reset/"}
"RESTORE" {:fn-name "restore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key ttl serialized-value & args], :fn-params-fixed [key ttl serialized-value], :req-args-fixed ["RESTORE" key ttl serialized-value], :fn-docstring "`RESTORE` Redis command.\n\nCreates a key from the serialized representation of a value.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(1) to create the new key and additional O(N*M) to reconstruct the serialized value, where N is the number of Redis objects composing the value and M their average size. For small string values the time complexity is thus O(1)+O(1*M) where M is small, so simply O(1). However for sorted set values the complexity is O(N*M*log(N)) because inserting values into sorted sets is O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/restore/"}
"RESTORE-ASKING" {:fn-name "restore-asking", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key ttl serialized-value & args], :fn-params-fixed [key ttl serialized-value], :req-args-fixed ["RESTORE-ASKING" key ttl serialized-value], :fn-docstring "`RESTORE-ASKING` Redis command.\n\nAn internal command for migrating keys in a cluster.\n\nSince Redis 3.0.0. Complexity: O(1) to create the new key and additional O(N*M) to reconstruct the serialized value, where N is the number of Redis objects composing the value and M their average size. For small string values the time complexity is thus O(1)+O(1*M) where M is small, so simply O(1). However for sorted set values the complexity is O(N*M*log(N)) because inserting values into sorted sets is O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/restore-asking/"}
"ROLE" {:fn-name "role", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["ROLE"], :fn-docstring "`ROLE` Redis command.\n\nReturns the replication role.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.12. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/role/"}
"RPOP" {:fn-name "rpop", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["RPOP" key], :fn-docstring "`RPOP` Redis command.\n\nReturns and removes the last elements of a list. Deletes the list if the last element was popped.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of elements returned.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/rpop/"}
"RPOPLPUSH" {:fn-name "rpoplpush", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [source destination], :req-args-fixed ["RPOPLPUSH" source destination], :fn-docstring "`RPOPLPUSH` Redis command.\n\nReturns the last element of a list after removing and pushing it to another list. Deletes the list if the last element was popped.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/rpoplpush/"}
"RPUSH" {:fn-name "rpush", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key element & args], :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["RPUSH" key element], :fn-docstring "`RPUSH` Redis command.\n\nAppends one or more elements to a list. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1) for each element added, so O(N) to add N elements when the command is called with multiple arguments.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/rpush/"}
"RPUSHX" {:fn-name "rpushx", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key element & args], :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["RPUSHX" key element], :fn-docstring "`RPUSHX` Redis command.\n\nAppends an element to a list only when the list exists.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(1) for each element added, so O(N) to add N elements when the command is called with multiple arguments.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/rpushx/"}
"SADD" {:fn-name "sadd", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["SADD" key member], :fn-docstring "`SADD` Redis command.\n\nAdds one or more members to a set. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1) for each element added, so O(N) to add N elements when the command is called with multiple arguments.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sadd/"}
"SAVE" {:fn-name "save", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SAVE"], :fn-docstring "`SAVE` Redis command.\n\nSynchronously saves the database(s) to disk.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the total number of keys in all databases.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/save/"}
"SCAN" {:fn-name "scan", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [cursor & args], :fn-params-fixed [cursor], :req-args-fixed ["SCAN" cursor], :fn-docstring "`SCAN` Redis command.\n\nIterates over the key names in the database.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.0. Complexity: O(1) for every call. O(N) for a complete iteration, including enough command calls for the cursor to return back to 0. N is the number of elements inside the collection.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/scan/"}
"SCARD" {:fn-name "scard", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SCARD" key], :fn-docstring "`SCARD` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of members in a set.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/scard/"}
"SCRIPT" {:fn-name "script", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" arg1], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT` Redis command.\n\nA container for Lua scripts management commands.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: Depends on subcommand.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script/"}
"SCRIPT DEBUG" {:fn-name "script-debug", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [arg1], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" "DEBUG" arg1], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT DEBUG` Redis command.\n\nSets the debug mode of server-side Lua scripts.\n\nSince Redis 3.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script-debug/"}
"SCRIPT EXISTS" {:fn-name "script-exists", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more [sha1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [sha1], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" "EXISTS" sha1], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT EXISTS` Redis command.\n\nDetermines whether server-side Lua scripts exist in the script cache.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(N) with N being the number of scripts to check (so checking a single script is an O(1) operation).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script-exists/"}
"SCRIPT FLUSH" {:fn-name "script-flush", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more [& args], :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" "FLUSH"], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT FLUSH` Redis command.\n\nRemoves all server-side Lua scripts from the script cache.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(N) with N being the number of scripts in cache.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script-flush/"}
"SCRIPT HELP" {:fn-name "script-help", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" "HELP"], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT HELP` Redis command.\n\nReturns helpful text about the different subcommands.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script-help/"}
"SCRIPT KILL" {:fn-name "script-kill", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" "KILL"], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT KILL` Redis command.\n\nTerminates a server-side Lua script during execution.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script-kill/"}
"SCRIPT LOAD" {:fn-name "script-load", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [script], :req-args-fixed ["SCRIPT" "LOAD" script], :fn-docstring "`SCRIPT LOAD` Redis command.\n\nLoads a server-side Lua script to the script cache.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(N) with N being the length in bytes of the script body.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/script-load/"}
"SDIFF" {:fn-name "sdiff", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SDIFF" key], :fn-docstring "`SDIFF` Redis command.\n\nReturns the difference of multiple sets.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the total number of elements in all given sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sdiff/"}
"SDIFFSTORE" {:fn-name "sdiffstore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [destination key & args], :fn-params-fixed [destination key], :req-args-fixed ["SDIFFSTORE" destination key], :fn-docstring "`SDIFFSTORE` Redis command.\n\nStores the difference of multiple sets in a key.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the total number of elements in all given sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sdiffstore/"}
"SELECT" {:fn-name "select", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [index], :req-args-fixed ["SELECT" index], :fn-docstring "`SELECT` Redis command.\n\nChanges the selected database.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/select/"}
"SET" {:fn-name "set", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key value & args], :fn-params-fixed [key value], :req-args-fixed ["SET" key value], :fn-docstring "`SET` Redis command.\n\nSets the string value of a key, ignoring its type. The key is created if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/set/"}
"SETBIT" {:fn-name "setbit", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key offset value], :req-args-fixed ["SETBIT" key offset value], :fn-docstring "`SETBIT` Redis command.\n\nSets or clears the bit at offset of the string value. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/setbit/"}
"SETEX" {:fn-name "setex", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key seconds value], :req-args-fixed ["SETEX" key seconds value], :fn-docstring "`SETEX` Redis command.\n\nSets the string value and expiration time of a key. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/setex/"}
"SETNX" {:fn-name "setnx", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key value], :req-args-fixed ["SETNX" key value], :fn-docstring "`SETNX` Redis command.\n\nSet the string value of a key only when the key doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/setnx/"}
"SETRANGE" {:fn-name "setrange", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key offset value], :req-args-fixed ["SETRANGE" key offset value], :fn-docstring "`SETRANGE` Redis command.\n\nOverwrites a part of a string value with another by an offset. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(1), not counting the time taken to copy the new string in place. Usually, this string is very small so the amortized complexity is O(1). Otherwise, complexity is O(M) with M being the length of the value argument.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/setrange/"}
"SHUTDOWN" {:fn-name "shutdown", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [& args], :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SHUTDOWN"], :fn-docstring "`SHUTDOWN` Redis command.\n\nSynchronously saves the database(s) to disk and shuts down the Redis server.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) when saving, where N is the total number of keys in all databases when saving data, otherwise O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/shutdown/"}
"SINTER" {:fn-name "sinter", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SINTER" key], :fn-docstring "`SINTER` Redis command.\n\nReturns the intersect of multiple sets.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N*M) worst case where N is the cardinality of the smallest set and M is the number of sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sinter/"}
"SINTERCARD" {:fn-name "sintercard", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["SINTERCARD" numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`SINTERCARD` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of members of the intersect of multiple sets.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(N*M) worst case where N is the cardinality of the smallest set and M is the number of sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sintercard/"}
"SINTERSTORE" {:fn-name "sinterstore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [destination key & args], :fn-params-fixed [destination key], :req-args-fixed ["SINTERSTORE" destination key], :fn-docstring "`SINTERSTORE` Redis command.\n\nStores the intersect of multiple sets in a key.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N*M) worst case where N is the cardinality of the smallest set and M is the number of sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sinterstore/"}
"SISMEMBER" {:fn-name "sismember", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["SISMEMBER" key member], :fn-docstring "`SISMEMBER` Redis command.\n\nDetermines whether a member belongs to a set.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sismember/"}
"SLAVEOF" {:fn-name "slaveof", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [arg1 arg2], :req-args-fixed ["SLAVEOF" arg1 arg2], :fn-docstring "`SLAVEOF` Redis command.\n\nSets a Redis server as a replica of another, or promotes it to being a master.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/slaveof/"}
"SLOWLOG" {:fn-name "slowlog", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1], :req-args-fixed ["SLOWLOG" arg1], :fn-docstring "`SLOWLOG` Redis command.\n\nA container for slow log commands.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.12. Complexity: Depends on subcommand.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/slowlog/"}
"SLOWLOG GET" {:fn-name "slowlog-get", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more [& args], :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SLOWLOG" "GET"], :fn-docstring "`SLOWLOG GET` Redis command.\n\nReturns the slow log's entries.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.12. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of entries returned.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/slowlog-get/"}
"SLOWLOG HELP" {:fn-name "slowlog-help", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SLOWLOG" "HELP"], :fn-docstring "`SLOWLOG HELP` Redis command.\n\nShow helpful text about the different subcommands.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/slowlog-help/"}
"SLOWLOG LEN" {:fn-name "slowlog-len", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SLOWLOG" "LEN"], :fn-docstring "`SLOWLOG LEN` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of entries in the slow log.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.12. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/slowlog-len/"}
"SLOWLOG RESET" {:fn-name "slowlog-reset", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SLOWLOG" "RESET"], :fn-docstring "`SLOWLOG RESET` Redis command.\n\nClears all entries from the slow log.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.12. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of entries in the slowlog.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/slowlog-reset/"}
"SMEMBERS" {:fn-name "smembers", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SMEMBERS" key], :fn-docstring "`SMEMBERS` Redis command.\n\nReturns all members of a set.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the set cardinality.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/smembers/"}
"SMISMEMBER" {:fn-name "smismember", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["SMISMEMBER" key member], :fn-docstring "`SMISMEMBER` Redis command.\n\nDetermines whether multiple members belong to a set.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of elements being checked for membership.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/smismember/"}
"SMOVE" {:fn-name "smove", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [source destination member], :req-args-fixed ["SMOVE" source destination member], :fn-docstring "`SMOVE` Redis command.\n\nMoves a member from one set to another.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/smove/"}
"SORT" {:fn-name "sort", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SORT" key], :fn-docstring "`SORT` Redis command.\n\nSorts the elements in a list, a set, or a sorted set, optionally storing the result.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N+M*log(M)) where N is the number of elements in the list or set to sort, and M the number of returned elements. When the elements are not sorted, complexity is O(N).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sort/"}
"SORT_RO" {:fn-name "sort_ro", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SORT_RO" key], :fn-docstring "`SORT_RO` Redis command.\n\nReturns the sorted elements of a list, a set, or a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(N+M*log(M)) where N is the number of elements in the list or set to sort, and M the number of returned elements. When the elements are not sorted, complexity is O(N).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sort_ro/"}
"SPOP" {:fn-name "spop", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SPOP" key], :fn-docstring "`SPOP` Redis command.\n\nReturns one or more random members from a set after removing them. Deletes the set if the last member was popped.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: Without the count argument O(1), otherwise O(N) where N is the value of the passed count.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/spop/"}
"SPUBLISH" {:fn-name "spublish", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [shardchannel message], :req-args-fixed ["SPUBLISH" shardchannel message], :fn-docstring "`SPUBLISH` Redis command.\n\nPost a message to a shard channel.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of clients subscribed to the receiving shard channel.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/spublish/"}
"SRANDMEMBER" {:fn-name "srandmember", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SRANDMEMBER" key], :fn-docstring "`SRANDMEMBER` Redis command.\n\nGet one or multiple random members from a set.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: Without the count argument O(1), otherwise O(N) where N is the absolute value of the passed count.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/srandmember/"}
"SREM" {:fn-name "srem", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["SREM" key member], :fn-docstring "`SREM` Redis command.\n\nRemoves one or more members from a set. Deletes the set if the last member was removed.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of members to be removed.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/srem/"}
"SSCAN" {:fn-name "sscan", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key cursor & args], :fn-params-fixed [key cursor], :req-args-fixed ["SSCAN" key cursor], :fn-docstring "`SSCAN` Redis command.\n\nIterates over members of a set.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.0. Complexity: O(1) for every call. O(N) for a complete iteration, including enough command calls for the cursor to return back to 0. N is the number of elements inside the collection.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sscan/"}
"SSUBSCRIBE" {:fn-name "ssubscribe", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [shardchannel & args], :fn-params-fixed [shardchannel], :req-args-fixed ["SSUBSCRIBE" shardchannel], :fn-docstring "`SSUBSCRIBE` Redis command.\n\nListens for messages published to shard channels.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of shard channels to subscribe to.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/ssubscribe/"}
"STRLEN" {:fn-name "strlen", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["STRLEN" key], :fn-docstring "`STRLEN` Redis command.\n\nReturns the length of a string value.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/strlen/"}
"SUBSCRIBE" {:fn-name "subscribe", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [channel & args], :fn-params-fixed [channel], :req-args-fixed ["SUBSCRIBE" channel], :fn-docstring "`SUBSCRIBE` Redis command.\n\nListens for messages published to channels.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of channels to subscribe to.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/subscribe/"}
"SUBSTR" {:fn-name "substr", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key start end], :req-args-fixed ["SUBSTR" key start end], :fn-docstring "`SUBSTR` Redis command.\n\nReturns a substring from a string value.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the length of the returned string. The complexity is ultimately determined by the returned length, but because creating a substring from an existing string is very cheap, it can be considered O(1) for small strings.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/substr/"}
"SUNION" {:fn-name "sunion", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["SUNION" key], :fn-docstring "`SUNION` Redis command.\n\nReturns the union of multiple sets.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the total number of elements in all given sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sunion/"}
"SUNIONSTORE" {:fn-name "sunionstore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [destination key & args], :fn-params-fixed [destination key], :req-args-fixed ["SUNIONSTORE" destination key], :fn-docstring "`SUNIONSTORE` Redis command.\n\nStores the union of multiple sets in a key.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the total number of elements in all given sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sunionstore/"}
"SUNSUBSCRIBE" {:fn-name "sunsubscribe", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [& args], :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SUNSUBSCRIBE"], :fn-docstring "`SUNSUBSCRIBE` Redis command.\n\nStops listening to messages posted to shard channels.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of shard channels to unsubscribe.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sunsubscribe/"}
"SWAPDB" {:fn-name "swapdb", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [index1 index2], :req-args-fixed ["SWAPDB" index1 index2], :fn-docstring "`SWAPDB` Redis command.\n\nSwaps two Redis databases.\n\nSince Redis 4.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the count of clients watching or blocking on keys from both databases.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/swapdb/"}
"SYNC" {:fn-name "sync", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["SYNC"], :fn-docstring "`SYNC` Redis command.\n\nAn internal command used in replication.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/sync/"}
"TIME" {:fn-name "time", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["TIME"], :fn-docstring "`TIME` Redis command.\n\nReturns the server time.\n\nSince Redis 2.6.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/time/"}
"TOUCH" {:fn-name "touch", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["TOUCH" key], :fn-docstring "`TOUCH` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of existing keys out of those specified after updating the time they were last accessed.\n\nSince Redis 3.2.1. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of keys that will be touched.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/touch/"}
"TRIMSLOTS" {:fn-name "trimslots", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4], :req-args-fixed ["TRIMSLOTS" arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4], :fn-docstring "`TRIMSLOTS` Redis command.\n\nTrim the keys that belong to specified slots.\n\nSince Redis 8.4.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the total number of keys in all databases.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/trimslots/"}
"TTL" {:fn-name "ttl", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["TTL" key], :fn-docstring "`TTL` Redis command.\n\nReturns the expiration time in seconds of a key.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/ttl/"}
"TYPE" {:fn-name "type", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["TYPE" key], :fn-docstring "`TYPE` Redis command.\n\nDetermines the type of value stored at a key.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/type/"}
"UNLINK" {:fn-name "unlink", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["UNLINK" key], :fn-docstring "`UNLINK` Redis command.\n\nAsynchronously deletes one or more keys.\n\nSince Redis 4.0.0. Complexity: O(1) for each key removed regardless of its size. Then the command does O(N) work in a different thread in order to reclaim memory, where N is the number of allocations the deleted objects where composed of.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/unlink/"}
"UNSUBSCRIBE" {:fn-name "unsubscribe", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [& args], :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["UNSUBSCRIBE"], :fn-docstring "`UNSUBSCRIBE` Redis command.\n\nStops listening to messages posted to channels.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of channels to unsubscribe.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/unsubscribe/"}
"UNWATCH" {:fn-name "unwatch", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["UNWATCH"], :fn-docstring "`UNWATCH` Redis command.\n\nForgets about watched keys of a transaction.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/unwatch/"}
"VADD" {:fn-name "vadd", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key arg1 arg2 arg3 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key arg1 arg2 arg3], :req-args-fixed ["VADD" key arg1 arg2 arg3], :fn-docstring "`VADD` Redis command.\n\nAdd one or more elements to a vector set, or update its vector if it already exists.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vadd/"}
"VCARD" {:fn-name "vcard", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["VCARD" key], :fn-docstring "`VCARD` Redis command.\n\nReturn the number of elements in a vector set.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vcard/"}
"VDIM" {:fn-name "vdim", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["VDIM" key], :fn-docstring "`VDIM` Redis command.\n\nReturn the dimension of vectors in the vector set.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vdim/"}
"VEMB" {:fn-name "vemb", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key element & args], :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["VEMB" key element], :fn-docstring "`VEMB` Redis command.\n\nReturn the vector associated with an element.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vemb/"}
"VGETATTR" {:fn-name "vgetattr", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["VGETATTR" key element], :fn-docstring "`VGETATTR` Redis command.\n\nRetrieve the JSON attributes of elements.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vgetattr/"}
"VINFO" {:fn-name "vinfo", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["VINFO" key], :fn-docstring "`VINFO` Redis command.\n\nReturn information about a vector set.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vinfo/"}
"VISMEMBER" {:fn-name "vismember", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["VISMEMBER" key element], :fn-docstring "`VISMEMBER` Redis command.\n\nCheck if an element exists in a vector set.\n\nSince Redis 8.2.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vismember/"}
"VLINKS" {:fn-name "vlinks", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key element & args], :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["VLINKS" key element], :fn-docstring "`VLINKS` Redis command.\n\nReturn the neighbors of an element at each layer in the HNSW graph.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vlinks/"}
"VRANDMEMBER" {:fn-name "vrandmember", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["VRANDMEMBER" key], :fn-docstring "`VRANDMEMBER` Redis command.\n\nReturn one or multiple random members from a vector set.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vrandmember/"}
"VRANGE" {:fn-name "vrange", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key start end & args], :fn-params-fixed [key start end], :req-args-fixed ["VRANGE" key start end], :fn-docstring "`VRANGE` Redis command.\n\nReturn vector set elements in a lex range.\n\nSince Redis 8.4.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vrange/"}
"VREM" {:fn-name "vrem", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key element], :req-args-fixed ["VREM" key element], :fn-docstring "`VREM` Redis command.\n\nRemove an element from a vector set.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vrem/"}
"VSETATTR" {:fn-name "vsetattr", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key element json], :req-args-fixed ["VSETATTR" key element json], :fn-docstring "`VSETATTR` Redis command.\n\nAssociate or remove the JSON attributes of elements.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vsetattr/"}
"VSIM" {:fn-name "vsim", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key arg1 arg2 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key arg1 arg2], :req-args-fixed ["VSIM" key arg1 arg2], :fn-docstring "`VSIM` Redis command.\n\nReturn elements by vector similarity.\n\nSince Redis 8.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/vsim/"}
"WAIT" {:fn-name "wait", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [numreplicas timeout], :req-args-fixed ["WAIT" numreplicas timeout], :fn-docstring "`WAIT` Redis command.\n\nBlocks until the asynchronous replication of all preceding write commands sent by the connection is completed.\n\nSince Redis 3.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/wait/"}
"WAITAOF" {:fn-name "waitaof", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [numlocal numreplicas timeout], :req-args-fixed ["WAITAOF" numlocal numreplicas timeout], :fn-docstring "`WAITAOF` Redis command.\n\nBlocks until all of the preceding write commands sent by the connection are written to the append-only file of the master and/or replicas.\n\nSince Redis 7.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/waitaof/"}
"WATCH" {:fn-name "watch", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["WATCH" key], :fn-docstring "`WATCH` Redis command.\n\nMonitors changes to keys to determine the execution of a transaction.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(1) for every key.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/watch/"}
"XACK" {:fn-name "xack", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key group id & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group id], :req-args-fixed ["XACK" key group id], :fn-docstring "`XACK` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of messages that were successfully acknowledged by the consumer group member of a stream.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1) for each message ID processed.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xack/"}
"XACKDEL" {:fn-name "xackdel", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key group arg1 arg2 arg3 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group arg1 arg2 arg3], :req-args-fixed ["XACKDEL" key group arg1 arg2 arg3], :fn-docstring "`XACKDEL` Redis command.\n\nAcknowledges and deletes one or multiple messages for a stream consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 8.2.0. Complexity: O(1) for each message ID processed.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xackdel/"}
"XADD" {:fn-name "xadd", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key arg1 arg2 arg3 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key arg1 arg2 arg3], :req-args-fixed ["XADD" key arg1 arg2 arg3], :fn-docstring "`XADD` Redis command.\n\nAppends a new message to a stream. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1) when adding a new entry, O(N) when trimming where N being the number of entries evicted.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xadd/"}
"XAUTOCLAIM" {:fn-name "xautoclaim", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key group consumer min-idle-time start & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group consumer min-idle-time start], :req-args-fixed ["XAUTOCLAIM" key group consumer min-idle-time start], :fn-docstring "`XAUTOCLAIM` Redis command.\n\nChanges, or acquires, ownership of messages in a consumer group, as if the messages were delivered to as consumer group member.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(1) if COUNT is small.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xautoclaim/"}
"XCFGSET" {:fn-name "xcfgset", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["XCFGSET" key], :fn-docstring "`XCFGSET` Redis command.\n\nSets the IDMP configuration parameters for a stream.\n\nSince Redis 8.6.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xcfgset/"}
"XCLAIM" {:fn-name "xclaim", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key group consumer min-idle-time id & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group consumer min-idle-time id], :req-args-fixed ["XCLAIM" key group consumer min-idle-time id], :fn-docstring "`XCLAIM` Redis command.\n\nChanges, or acquires, ownership of a message in a consumer group, as if the message was delivered a consumer group member.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(log N) with N being the number of messages in the PEL of the consumer group.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xclaim/"}
"XDEL" {:fn-name "xdel", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key id & args], :fn-params-fixed [key id], :req-args-fixed ["XDEL" key id], :fn-docstring "`XDEL` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of messages after removing them from a stream.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1) for each single item to delete in the stream, regardless of the stream size.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xdel/"}
"XDELEX" {:fn-name "xdelex", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key arg1 arg2 arg3 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key arg1 arg2 arg3], :req-args-fixed ["XDELEX" key arg1 arg2 arg3], :fn-docstring "`XDELEX` Redis command.\n\nDeletes one or multiple entries from the stream.\n\nSince Redis 8.2.0. Complexity: O(1) for each single item to delete in the stream, regardless of the stream size.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xdelex/"}
"XGROUP" {:fn-name "xgroup", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" arg1], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP` Redis command.\n\nA container for consumer groups commands.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: Depends on subcommand.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup/"}
"XGROUP CREATE" {:fn-name "xgroup-create", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more [key group arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group arg1], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" "CREATE" key group arg1], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP CREATE` Redis command.\n\nCreates a consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup-create/"}
"XGROUP CREATECONSUMER" {:fn-name "xgroup-createconsumer", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key group consumer], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" "CREATECONSUMER" key group consumer], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP CREATECONSUMER` Redis command.\n\nCreates a consumer in a consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup-createconsumer/"}
"XGROUP DELCONSUMER" {:fn-name "xgroup-delconsumer", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key group consumer], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" "DELCONSUMER" key group consumer], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP DELCONSUMER` Redis command.\n\nDeletes a consumer from a consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup-delconsumer/"}
"XGROUP DESTROY" {:fn-name "xgroup-destroy", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key group], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" "DESTROY" key group], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP DESTROY` Redis command.\n\nDestroys a consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of entries in the group's pending entries list (PEL).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup-destroy/"}
"XGROUP HELP" {:fn-name "xgroup-help", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" "HELP"], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP HELP` Redis command.\n\nReturns helpful text about the different subcommands.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup-help/"}
"XGROUP SETID" {:fn-name "xgroup-setid", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more [key group arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group arg1], :req-args-fixed ["XGROUP" "SETID" key group arg1], :fn-docstring "`XGROUP SETID` Redis command.\n\nSets the last-delivered ID of a consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xgroup-setid/"}
"XIDMPRECORD" {:fn-name "xidmprecord", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key pid iid stream-id], :req-args-fixed ["XIDMPRECORD" key pid iid stream-id], :fn-docstring "`XIDMPRECORD` Redis command.\n\nAn internal command for setting IDMP metadata on an existing stream message.\n\nSince Redis 8.6.2. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xidmprecord/"}
"XINFO" {:fn-name "xinfo", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1], :req-args-fixed ["XINFO" arg1], :fn-docstring "`XINFO` Redis command.\n\nA container for stream introspection commands.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: Depends on subcommand.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xinfo/"}
"XINFO CONSUMERS" {:fn-name "xinfo-consumers", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key group], :req-args-fixed ["XINFO" "CONSUMERS" key group], :fn-docstring "`XINFO CONSUMERS` Redis command.\n\nReturns a list of the consumers in a consumer group.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xinfo-consumers/"}
"XINFO GROUPS" {:fn-name "xinfo-groups", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["XINFO" "GROUPS" key], :fn-docstring "`XINFO GROUPS` Redis command.\n\nReturns a list of the consumer groups of a stream.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xinfo-groups/"}
"XINFO HELP" {:fn-name "xinfo-help", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [], :req-args-fixed ["XINFO" "HELP"], :fn-docstring "`XINFO HELP` Redis command.\n\nReturns helpful text about the different subcommands.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xinfo-help/"}
"XINFO STREAM" {:fn-name "xinfo-stream", :cluster-key-idx 2, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["XINFO" "STREAM" key], :fn-docstring "`XINFO STREAM` Redis command.\n\nReturns information about a stream.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xinfo-stream/"}
"XLEN" {:fn-name "xlen", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["XLEN" key], :fn-docstring "`XLEN` Redis command.\n\nReturn the number of messages in a stream.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xlen/"}
"XNACK" {:fn-name "xnack", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key group arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4], :req-args-fixed ["XNACK" key group arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4], :fn-docstring "`XNACK` Redis command.\n\nReleases claimed messages back to the group's PEL without acknowledging them, making them available for re-delivery.\n\nSince Redis 8.8.0. Complexity: O(1) for each message ID processed.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xnack/"}
"XPENDING" {:fn-name "xpending", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key group & args], :fn-params-fixed [key group], :req-args-fixed ["XPENDING" key group], :fn-docstring "`XPENDING` Redis command.\n\nReturns the information and entries from a stream consumer group's pending entries list.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(N) with N being the number of elements returned, so asking for a small fixed number of entries per call is O(1). O(M), where M is the total number of entries scanned when used with the IDLE filter. When the command returns just the summary and the list of consumers is small, it runs in O(1) time; otherwise, an additional O(N) time for iterating every consumer.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xpending/"}
"XRANGE" {:fn-name "xrange", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key start end & args], :fn-params-fixed [key start end], :req-args-fixed ["XRANGE" key start end], :fn-docstring "`XRANGE` Redis command.\n\nReturns the messages from a stream within a range of IDs.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(N) with N being the number of elements being returned. If N is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with COUNT), you can consider it O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xrange/"}
"XREAD" {:fn-name "xread", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 arg2 arg3 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1 arg2 arg3], :req-args-fixed ["XREAD" arg1 arg2 arg3], :fn-docstring "`XREAD` Redis command.\n\nReturns messages from multiple streams with IDs greater than the ones requested. Blocks until a message is available otherwise.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xread/"}
"XREADGROUP" {:fn-name "xreadgroup", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4 arg5 arg6 & args], :fn-params-fixed [arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4 arg5 arg6], :req-args-fixed ["XREADGROUP" arg1 arg2 arg3 arg4 arg5 arg6], :fn-docstring "`XREADGROUP` Redis command.\n\nReturns new or historical messages from a stream for a consumer in a group. Blocks until a message is available otherwise.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: For each stream mentioned: O(M) with M being the number of elements returned. If M is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with COUNT), you can consider it O(1). On the other side when XREADGROUP blocks, XADD will pay the O(N) time in order to serve the N clients blocked on the stream getting new data.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xreadgroup/"}
"XREVRANGE" {:fn-name "xrevrange", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key end start & args], :fn-params-fixed [key end start], :req-args-fixed ["XREVRANGE" key end start], :fn-docstring "`XREVRANGE` Redis command.\n\nReturns the messages from a stream within a range of IDs in reverse order.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(N) with N being the number of elements returned. If N is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with COUNT), you can consider it O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xrevrange/"}
"XSETID" {:fn-name "xsetid", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key last-id & args], :fn-params-fixed [key last-id], :req-args-fixed ["XSETID" key last-id], :fn-docstring "`XSETID` Redis command.\n\nAn internal command for replicating stream values.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xsetid/"}
"XTRIM" {:fn-name "xtrim", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key arg1 arg2 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key arg1 arg2], :req-args-fixed ["XTRIM" key arg1 arg2], :fn-docstring "`XTRIM` Redis command.\n\nDeletes messages from the beginning of a stream.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(N), with N being the number of evicted entries. Constant times are very small however, since entries are organized in macro nodes containing multiple entries that can be released with a single deallocation.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/xtrim/"}
"ZADD" {:fn-name "zadd", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key arg1 arg2 & args], :fn-params-fixed [key arg1 arg2], :req-args-fixed ["ZADD" key arg1 arg2], :fn-docstring "`ZADD` Redis command.\n\nAdds one or more members to a sorted set, or updates their scores. Creates the key if it doesn't exist.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)) for each item added, where N is the number of elements in the sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zadd/"}
"ZCARD" {:fn-name "zcard", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["ZCARD" key], :fn-docstring "`ZCARD` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of members in a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zcard/"}
"ZCOUNT" {:fn-name "zcount", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZCOUNT" key min max], :fn-docstring "`ZCOUNT` Redis command.\n\nReturns the count of members in a sorted set that have scores within a range.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(log(N)) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zcount/"}
"ZDIFF" {:fn-name "zdiff", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["ZDIFF" numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`ZDIFF` Redis command.\n\nReturns the difference between multiple sorted sets.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(L + (N-K)log(N)) worst case where L is the total number of elements in all the sets, N is the size of the first set, and K is the size of the result set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zdiff/"}
"ZDIFFSTORE" {:fn-name "zdiffstore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [destination numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [destination numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["ZDIFFSTORE" destination numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`ZDIFFSTORE` Redis command.\n\nStores the difference of multiple sorted sets in a key.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(L + (N-K)log(N)) worst case where L is the total number of elements in all the sets, N is the size of the first set, and K is the size of the result set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zdiffstore/"}
"ZINCRBY" {:fn-name "zincrby", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key increment member], :req-args-fixed ["ZINCRBY" key increment member], :fn-docstring "`ZINCRBY` Redis command.\n\nIncrements the score of a member in a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)) where N is the number of elements in the sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zincrby/"}
"ZINTER" {:fn-name "zinter", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["ZINTER" numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`ZINTER` Redis command.\n\nReturns the intersect of multiple sorted sets.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(N*K)+O(M*log(M)) worst case with N being the smallest input sorted set, K being the number of input sorted sets and M being the number of elements in the resulting sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zinter/"}
"ZINTERCARD" {:fn-name "zintercard", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["ZINTERCARD" numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`ZINTERCARD` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of members of the intersect of multiple sorted sets.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(N*K) worst case with N being the smallest input sorted set, K being the number of input sorted sets.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zintercard/"}
"ZINTERSTORE" {:fn-name "zinterstore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [destination numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [destination numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["ZINTERSTORE" destination numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`ZINTERSTORE` Redis command.\n\nStores the intersect of multiple sorted sets in a key.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(N*K)+O(M*log(M)) worst case with N being the smallest input sorted set, K being the number of input sorted sets and M being the number of elements in the resulting sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zinterstore/"}
"ZLEXCOUNT" {:fn-name "zlexcount", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZLEXCOUNT" key min max], :fn-docstring "`ZLEXCOUNT` Redis command.\n\nReturns the number of members in a sorted set within a lexicographical range.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.9. Complexity: O(log(N)) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zlexcount/"}
"ZMPOP" {:fn-name "zmpop", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [numkeys key arg1 & args], :fn-params-fixed [numkeys key arg1], :req-args-fixed ["ZMPOP" numkeys key arg1], :fn-docstring "`ZMPOP` Redis command.\n\nReturns the highest- or lowest-scoring members from one or more sorted sets after removing them. Deletes the sorted set if the last member was popped.\n\nSince Redis 7.0.0. Complexity: O(K) + O(M*log(N)) where K is the number of provided keys, N being the number of elements in the sorted set, and M being the number of elements popped.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zmpop/"}
"ZMSCORE" {:fn-name "zmscore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["ZMSCORE" key member], :fn-docstring "`ZMSCORE` Redis command.\n\nReturns the score of one or more members in a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of members being requested.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zmscore/"}
"ZPOPMAX" {:fn-name "zpopmax", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["ZPOPMAX" key], :fn-docstring "`ZPOPMAX` Redis command.\n\nReturns the highest-scoring members from a sorted set after removing them. Deletes the sorted set if the last member was popped.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(log(N)*M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set, and M being the number of elements popped.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zpopmax/"}
"ZPOPMIN" {:fn-name "zpopmin", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["ZPOPMIN" key], :fn-docstring "`ZPOPMIN` Redis command.\n\nReturns the lowest-scoring members from a sorted set after removing them. Deletes the sorted set if the last member was popped.\n\nSince Redis 5.0.0. Complexity: O(log(N)*M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set, and M being the number of elements popped.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zpopmin/"}
"ZRANDMEMBER" {:fn-name "zrandmember", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key & args], :fn-params-fixed [key], :req-args-fixed ["ZRANDMEMBER" key], :fn-docstring "`ZRANDMEMBER` Redis command.\n\nReturns one or more random members from a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(N) where N is the number of members returned.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrandmember/"}
"ZRANGE" {:fn-name "zrange", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key start stop & args], :fn-params-fixed [key start stop], :req-args-fixed ["ZRANGE" key start stop], :fn-docstring "`ZRANGE` Redis command.\n\nReturns members in a sorted set within a range of indexes.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements returned.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrange/"}
"ZRANGEBYLEX" {:fn-name "zrangebylex", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key min max & args], :fn-params-fixed [key min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZRANGEBYLEX" key min max], :fn-docstring "`ZRANGEBYLEX` Redis command.\n\nReturns members in a sorted set within a lexicographical range.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.9. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements being returned. If M is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with LIMIT), you can consider it O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrangebylex/"}
"ZRANGEBYSCORE" {:fn-name "zrangebyscore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key min max & args], :fn-params-fixed [key min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZRANGEBYSCORE" key min max], :fn-docstring "`ZRANGEBYSCORE` Redis command.\n\nReturns members in a sorted set within a range of scores.\n\nSince Redis 1.0.5. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements being returned. If M is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with LIMIT), you can consider it O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrangebyscore/"}
"ZRANGESTORE" {:fn-name "zrangestore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [dst src min max & args], :fn-params-fixed [dst src min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZRANGESTORE" dst src min max], :fn-docstring "`ZRANGESTORE` Redis command.\n\nStores a range of members from sorted set in a key.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements stored into the destination key.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrangestore/"}
"ZRANK" {:fn-name "zrank", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["ZRANK" key member], :fn-docstring "`ZRANK` Redis command.\n\nReturns the index of a member in a sorted set ordered by ascending scores.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrank/"}
"ZREM" {:fn-name "zrem", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["ZREM" key member], :fn-docstring "`ZREM` Redis command.\n\nRemoves one or more members from a sorted set. Deletes the sorted set if all members were removed.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(M*log(N)) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements to be removed.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrem/"}
"ZREMRANGEBYLEX" {:fn-name "zremrangebylex", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZREMRANGEBYLEX" key min max], :fn-docstring "`ZREMRANGEBYLEX` Redis command.\n\nRemoves members in a sorted set within a lexicographical range. Deletes the sorted set if all members were removed.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.9. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements removed by the operation.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zremrangebylex/"}
"ZREMRANGEBYRANK" {:fn-name "zremrangebyrank", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key start stop], :req-args-fixed ["ZREMRANGEBYRANK" key start stop], :fn-docstring "`ZREMRANGEBYRANK` Redis command.\n\nRemoves members in a sorted set within a range of indexes. Deletes the sorted set if all members were removed.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements removed by the operation.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zremrangebyrank/"}
"ZREMRANGEBYSCORE" {:fn-name "zremrangebyscore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key min max], :req-args-fixed ["ZREMRANGEBYSCORE" key min max], :fn-docstring "`ZREMRANGEBYSCORE` Redis command.\n\nRemoves members in a sorted set within a range of scores. Deletes the sorted set if all members were removed.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements removed by the operation.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zremrangebyscore/"}
"ZREVRANGE" {:fn-name "zrevrange", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key start stop & args], :fn-params-fixed [key start stop], :req-args-fixed ["ZREVRANGE" key start stop], :fn-docstring "`ZREVRANGE` Redis command.\n\nReturns members in a sorted set within a range of indexes in reverse order.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements returned.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrevrange/"}
"ZREVRANGEBYLEX" {:fn-name "zrevrangebylex", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key max min & args], :fn-params-fixed [key max min], :req-args-fixed ["ZREVRANGEBYLEX" key max min], :fn-docstring "`ZREVRANGEBYLEX` Redis command.\n\nReturns members in a sorted set within a lexicographical range in reverse order.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.9. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements being returned. If M is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with LIMIT), you can consider it O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrevrangebylex/"}
"ZREVRANGEBYSCORE" {:fn-name "zrevrangebyscore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key max min & args], :fn-params-fixed [key max min], :req-args-fixed ["ZREVRANGEBYSCORE" key max min], :fn-docstring "`ZREVRANGEBYSCORE` Redis command.\n\nReturns members in a sorted set within a range of scores in reverse order.\n\nSince Redis 2.2.0. Complexity: O(log(N)+M) with N being the number of elements in the sorted set and M the number of elements being returned. If M is constant (e.g. always asking for the first 10 elements with LIMIT), you can consider it O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrevrangebyscore/"}
"ZREVRANK" {:fn-name "zrevrank", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key member & args], :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["ZREVRANK" key member], :fn-docstring "`ZREVRANK` Redis command.\n\nReturns the index of a member in a sorted set ordered by descending scores.\n\nSince Redis 2.0.0. Complexity: O(log(N)).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zrevrank/"}
"ZSCAN" {:fn-name "zscan", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [key cursor & args], :fn-params-fixed [key cursor], :req-args-fixed ["ZSCAN" key cursor], :fn-docstring "`ZSCAN` Redis command.\n\nIterates over members and scores of a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 2.8.0. Complexity: O(1) for every call. O(N) for a complete iteration, including enough command calls for the cursor to return back to 0. N is the number of elements inside the collection.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zscan/"}
"ZSCORE" {:fn-name "zscore", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more nil, :fn-params-fixed [key member], :req-args-fixed ["ZSCORE" key member], :fn-docstring "`ZSCORE` Redis command.\n\nReturns the score of a member in a sorted set.\n\nSince Redis 1.2.0. Complexity: O(1).\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zscore/"}
"ZUNION" {:fn-name "zunion", :cluster-key-idx 1, :fn-params-more [numkeys key & args], :fn-params-fixed [numkeys key], :req-args-fixed ["ZUNION" numkeys key], :fn-docstring "`ZUNION` Redis command.\n\nReturns the union of multiple sorted sets.\n\nSince Redis 6.2.0. Complexity: O(N)+O(M*log(M)) with N being the sum of the sizes of the input sorted sets, and M being the number of elements in the resulting sorted set.\n\nReference: https://redis.io/commands/zunion/"}
